  "narrative": "The three strongest binary associations are now independently validated in this dataset: feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001, while feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are associated with higher outcome_001. The next high-information step is to determine whether these associations are approximately additive across the three predictors or whether one predictor modifies the effect of another. The all-positive triple cell feature_002=1/feature_037=1/feature_010=1 is too sparse to support a valid mean-difference cell, so the most decisive new comparisons are pairwise interactions restricted to the large stratum in which the third predictor is absent. I registered feature_002 by feature_037 interaction within feature_010=0, feature_002 by feature_010 interaction within feature_037=0, and feature_010 by feature_037 interaction within feature_002=0. These use four valid cells and test whether apparent pairwise interactions are genuine or driven by the sparse triple-overlap region. The anticipated directions are based on earlier conditional estimates: feature_002 appears slightly attenuated when feature_037=1 among feature_010=0 individuals, feature_002 appears amplified when feature_010=1 among feature_037=0 individuals, and feature_010 appears slightly attenuated when feature_037=1 among feature_002=0 individuals. These claims remain exploratory; a null or small interaction would support approximate additivity, while a meaningful interaction would indicate conditional heterogeneity. To broaden the search without re-mixing the dominant predictor structure, I also registered screens of untested binary flags within the large reference stratum feature_002=0, feature_037=0, feature_010=0. These tests ask whether feature_033, feature_063, feature_043, or feature_017 have associations in a stratum where the three accepted strong predictors are absent. The expected direction was set to uncertain because these flags have no assigned biological role; the proposed claim direction is negative, i.e. flag=1 associated with stronger dependency, but large positive raw associations would be interpreted as evidence against the proposed direction and would motivate a reversed claim if warranted. Finally, I registered two biomarker-interaction screens for feature_002 and feature_010 with standardized research signatures feature_018 and feature_036, testing whether high versus low signature values modify the strong positive associations. All statements are associations in the supplied dataset, not causal effects or generalizable biological claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported dataset associations: H6 accepted/closed/validated: feature_037=1 lowers outcome_001 / stronger dependency, raw about -0.83 to -0.85. H13 accepted/closed/validated: feature_010=1 raises outcome_001 / weaker dependency, raw about +0.42 discovery and +0.36 validation. H14 accepted/closed/validated: feature_010 persists among feature_037=0. H35 accepted/closed/validated: feature_002=1 raises outcome_001 / weaker dependency, raw about +0.83 discovery and +0.83 validation; H18 remains rejected. Conditional persistence accepted: H46, H36-H39, H43, H49-H50 for feature_002; H47-H48, H51-H52, H15/H24, H23 for feature_037/feature_010. Active architecture tests: H40-H45 and H53-H56. The all-positive triple cell feature_002=1/feature_037=1/feature_010=1 is too sparse for valid two-cell mean differences. New registered comparisons target valid pairwise interactions within the third predictor absent stratum, plus residual-stratum screens of untested binary flags in feature_002=0/feature_037=0/feature_010=0 and two signature-interaction screens. Interpretation: if conditional interactions are small, treat the three main effects as approximate dataset additive associations; if large, report conditional heterogeneity and consider validation of the affected stratum estimates. Residual-stratum screens should not be interpreted as independent biological markers unless they survive validation. Limitations: all are descriptive dataset associations; conditional estimates share overlapping observations and do not prove causal adjustments; generalizability remains uncertain. Negative: H1-H4, H7, H8-H12, H16-H22, H25. Near-threshold H20/H21 not promoted. Deferred/broad: H26-H34 remain available but lower priority than architecture; signature interactions with accepted binary predictors are now partly expanded."
